Task 2: Spring Boot Data JPA – Digital Library Cover Image Management System (BLOB)
Scenario
Develop a Spring Boot application for a Digital Library where each book has a cover image. Since
images are binary data, store them using BLOB.
Entity Class: LibraryBook
bookId : Long
bookTitle : String
authorName : String
coverImage : byte[] (BLOB)
Requirements
Entity Layer- Create an entity class named LibraryBook.- Use @Entity and @Table.- Mark bookId as primary key using @Id.- Store image data using:
@Lob
@Column(columnDefinition = "BLOB")
private byte[] coverImage;
Repository Layer
Create LibraryBookRepository extending:
JpaRepository<LibraryBook, Long>
Service Layer
Implement methods:
1. Save Book Details with Cover Image
2. Find Book By Id
3. View All Books
4. Delete Book
Runner Class
Using CommandLineRunner:- Read image files from local system.- Convert images into byte arrays.- Store 3 book records with cover images.- Retrieve and display book information.- Display image size using book.getCoverImage().length
